INFO  [Claude Code] ## Summary
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] I've successfully resolved the Diffblue Cover test generation issue (Issue 1, severity 0) for the `OfficePluginManager` class. The problem was that the Spring test context failed to initialize because `OfficePluginManager` requires an actual LibreOffice/OpenOffice installation, which isn't available in the test environment.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Solution Implemented
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] I created a comprehensive test configuration with three components:
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] 1. **TestOfficeConfig.java** (server/src/test/java/cn/keking/config/TestOfficeConfig.java):
INFO  [Claude Code]    - A Spring `@TestConfiguration` that provides a mock `OfficePluginManager` bean
INFO  [Claude Code]    - Uses `@Primary` annotation to ensure the mock takes precedence over the real bean during tests
INFO  [Claude Code]    - This prevents the actual office manager initialization that requires real office installation
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] 2. **DiffblueTestBase.java** (server/src/test/java/cn/keking/DiffblueTestBase.java):
INFO  [Claude Code]    - A custom base class that imports `TestOfficeConfig`
INFO  [Claude Code]    - All Diffblue-generated tests can extend this class to automatically get the mock configuration
INFO  [Claude Code]    - Configured in `.diffblue/create.args` with `--base-class cn.keking.DiffblueTestBase`
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] 3. **application-test.properties** (server/src/test/resources/application-test.properties):
INFO  [Claude Code]    - Test-specific configuration file
INFO  [Claude Code]    - Provides minimal configuration for office plugin settings
INFO  [Claude Code]    - Disables cache and sets up test-friendly defaults
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Files Created/Modified
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Created**: `server/src/test/java/cn/keking/config/TestOfficeConfig.java`
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Created**: `server/src/test/java/cn/keking/DiffblueTestBase.java`
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Created**: `server/src/test/resources/application-test.properties`
INFO  [Claude Code] - **Modified**: `.diffblue/create.args` (added `--base-class cn.keking.DiffblueTestBase`)
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] ### Next Steps
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] As mentioned in your advisory note, you should run:
INFO  [Claude Code] ```bash
INFO  [Claude Code] mvn install -DskipTests
INFO  [Claude Code] ```
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] This will ensure the classpath is updated with the new test configuration files. After this, Diffblue Cover should be able to generate tests for `OfficePluginManager.destroyOfficeManager()` and other methods without encountering the bean instantiation exception.
INFO  [Claude Code] 
INFO  [Claude Code] The solution follows the Diffblue best practice of using a custom base class (as referenced in the R026 documentation link) and provides a clean, maintainable way to mock Spring beans that have complex initialization requirements.
